  "briefing": "## Situation\nMidday in January, dense fog over the plains: visibility about 800 m. The camera will not see anything beyond that, in daylight or thermal. Our own patrol drones are up, and birds are working the fields.\n## Mission\nDetect, identify and defeat hostile drones before they reach Post Alpha. Leave birds, civilians and friendlies alone.\n## ROE\nWEAPONS TIGHT — intercept only tracks you have classified as a threat type and declared HOSTILE. No intercepts inside the marked no-kinetic zones (settlements).\n## Assets\n- Radar, EO/IR camera and RF detector on high ground near the asset\n- RF jammer, 2.0 km, ±10° sector, 10 s cycle\n- GNSS spoofer, 2.0 km, ±10° sector, 15 s cycle\n- Interceptor, 1.5 km, 9 rounds, 6 s reload\n## Intel\nThe radar and the RF detector are your eyes today. Use track behaviour (speed, height, heading toward the post) and RF to sort contacts early: by the time the camera can identify something, it is under a kilometre out.",
